        "question": {
          ":question/id": "9d7077fc-b0a2-515f-bdaf-fece2a947de8",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=4 \\\\  y-3z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5z &=2 \\\\  y-3z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5z+2 \\\\  y &=3z-1 \\\\  z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5z+2 \\\\ 3z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
